2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #Key Issues Found
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #• 1. `writepng.cpp` has bugs*
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #- The buffer conversion logic is confusing and likely incorrect.
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #- It's writing `bgrBuffer` (which is being treated as BGRA) while `png_set_bgr` is enabled.
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #- The alpha handling is hardcoded to 255 inside the row loop, which is inefficient.
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #- The function signature suggests `bgrBuffer` is a scratch buffer, but the usage is fragile.
2294b785 [grok-build-0.1] #
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #• 2. Dead / commented code*
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #- Heavy use of commented-out code (especially FreeType and macOS snapshot).
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #- `initFreetype` is called in `win32snapshot.cpp` but never used.
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #• 3. Inconsistent image writing*
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #- `writeImageFile` behaves differently between Windows and macOS versions (Windows writes BMP + JPG
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #+ PNG, macOS skips BMP).
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #• 4. Platform split*
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #- The snapshot functionality is heavily duplicated between `win32snapshot.cpp` and
2294b786 [grok-build-0.1] #`macossnapshot.cpp`.
