22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #Suggestions
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #1. Add a `write(address, value)` method (symmetric to `read`) and route all stores through
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #it. This will become important once you emulate more hardware (Pokey, trackball, etc.).
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #2. Make tracing optional. The current loop does a lot of string work every instruction.
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #Something like:
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #   const trace = true; // or controlled by flag
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #   if (trace) { console.log(...) }
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #3. Extract opcode handlers into named functions once you have more than ~30-40 opcodes. The
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #giant switch is getting hard to navigate.
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #4. Consider a small `Cpu6502` class separate from `Machine`. The current class is doing
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #both CPU + system.
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #5. Fix the labels line and also make `setLabels` accept the right type:
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #   setLabels(labels: Map<string, string>)
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #Quick Wins
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like me to:
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #- A. Give you a cleaned-up version of the JSR + stack handling?
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #- B. Suggest a structure for adding a proper `write()` method + hardware dispatch?
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #- C. Help identify which opcodes Centipede is currently hitting that are missing (by
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #running it with better logging)?
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #- D. Review the timing / vblank / interrupt logic more closely?
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #Just say which direction you'd like to go.
22e0820c [grok-build-0.1] #
