230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.049 64.56KB 6.21s
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #Thanks for sharing. This is a substantial TypeScript 6502 arcade-machine emulator/debugger, with:
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- ROM loading for Centipede and Asteroids.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A partially implemented Digital Vector Generator for Asteroids.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Terminal-based memory/display inspection for Centipede.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Interactive single-step / continuous execution controls.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- IRQ/vblank handling and input-mapped memory reads.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A growing opcode interpreter, including common indexed, indirect, stack, arithmetic, branch, and
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #bit operations.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Trace output with labels, register status, cycle count, and a compact braille memory display.
230678ba [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #A few things that stand out:
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `reset` declares four parameters (`address, irq, reset, vectors`), but the `R` key path calls it
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #with three. TypeScript should flag that, and it may leave `hasDVG` as `undefined`.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Several members are used without visible declarations on `Machine`, such as `cyclecount` and
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #`hasDVG`. This is fine only when strict property checking is not enabled.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Some instructions still write directly to `memory`, while others go through `writeAddress`. For
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #an emulator with memory-mapped hardware, routing all writes through `writeAddress` will
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #matter—particularly `STA ($nn),Y`, absolute `INC`/`DEC`, and absolute `LSR`.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `tick()` advances by a fixed four cycles per instruction. That is a sensible temporary execution
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #clock, but it will make vblank timing and timing-sensitive ROM behaviour approximate until
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #individual opcode cycle counts, plus branch/page-cross penalties, are represented.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The DVG decoder is clearly exploratory, especially `LABS` and the vector semantics, but the
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #instruction loop, banking choice, and control-flow operations give it a useful foundation.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `VectorGenerator` would eventually benefit from stack bounds checks: DVG calls can underflow or
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #overflow its eight-entry stack when decoding goes wrong.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #Overall, it is a nicely direct, inspectable emulator rather than an overly abstract one—the trace
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #tooling and ROM labels should make bringing up additional opcodes and diagnosing game behaviour
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #much easier.
230678bb [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067b42 [simon@midnightblue.local] any issues with 6502 carry operations?
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.065 66.86KB 14.33s
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #The binary-mode carry logic is mostly sound. `ADC`, `SBC`, comparisons, shifts, rotates, and carry
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #branches generally handle C correctly.
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #Key issues:
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Decimal mode is not implemented.
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	`SED` and `CLD` modify D, but every `ADC` and `SBC` implementation still uses binary arithmetic.
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #On an NMOS 6502, D changes the result and carry behavior for those operations. If either ROM uses
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #BCD arithmetic, results and C will be wrong.
23067c2d [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `SBC` overflow logic is wrong in every implemented SBC addressing mode.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	This affects `SBC #imm`, zero page, zero page X, and absolute Y. The code calculates V using the
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #complemented operand used internally for addition. For subtraction, overflow must be determined
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #using the original operand being subtracted.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	This does not change C itself, but can cause `BVS` / `BVC` to branch incorrectly after `SBC`.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The actual `SBC` carry/no-borrow calculation is correct in binary mode.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	The implementation using `A + (operand ^ 0xFF) + C`, followed by setting C when the intermediate
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #result exceeds `0xFF`, is correct. The comment saying “result is >= 0” is misleading, but the
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #implementation is fine.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `setCarry` expects a boolean, but ASL passes a number.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	In the accumulator ASL implementation, `carry` is `0` or `1` and is passed directly to `setCarry`.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #JavaScript handles it correctly through truthiness, but TypeScript should object under normal
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #checking. This is a typing/clarity issue rather than an emulation bug.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Carry-sensitive instructions otherwise look correct:
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `CLC` / `SEC`: correct.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `CMP`, `CPX`, `CPY`: correctly set C when register ≥ operand.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `LSR`: C receives old bit 0.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `ASL`: C receives old bit 7.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `ROL` and `ROR`: use old C as incoming bit and set C from the shifted-out bit.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `BCC` / `BCS`: conditions are correct.
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23067c2e [gpt-5.6-terra] #One adjacent status-register bug worth fixing: `RTI` currently masks with `~0x14`, which clears
23067c2f [gpt-5.6-terra] #both B and I. RTI must restore I from the status byte it pulled; clearing I unconditionally
23067c2f [gpt-5.6-terra] #can change interrupt behavior. It is not a carry bug, but it will make status restoration
23067c2f [gpt-5.6-terra] #inaccurate.
23067c2f [gpt-5.6-terra] #
