2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The `adc(value)` refactor is a good change: it centralizes the NMOS decimal handling, carry,
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #overflow, A update, and N/Z behavior. The migrated `ADC $zp` path should behave correctly.
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The new `sbc(value)` helper also fixes the earlier binary SBC overflow issue. Its overflow
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #expression now uses the original operand:
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #(a ^ result) & (a ^ value) & $80
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #That is the correct binary subtraction overflow rule. Its binary carry/no-borrow calculation is
2306e412 [gpt-5.6-terra] #also correct.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #However, unlike `adc`, the `decimal` variable in `sbc` is presently unused:
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #const decimal=(st&8)==8;
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #So `SBC #imm`—the only SBC case currently routed through the helper—is still binary arithmetic
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #under `SED`. Its future BCD path needs subtraction-specific decimal adjustment; it cannot reuse
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #ADC’s `+ 06` / `+ 60` logic unchanged.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Other current observations:
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Only `ADC $zp` uses `adc(value)` so far. The immediate, indexed, absolute, and indirect ADC
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #opcodes remain binary-only until migrated.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Only `SBC #imm` uses `sbc(value)` so far. The zero-page, zero-page-X, and absolute-Y cases retain
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #their old logic, including the old incorrect V calculation.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `adc` correctly calculates `N` and `Z` from `sum & $ff`, which is the NMOS 6502 behavior in
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #decimal mode.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `sbc` currently calculates N/Z from the stored result. That is fine in binary mode. For NMOS
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #decimal SBC, N/Z should likewise eventually come from the unadjusted binary result rather than the
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #BCD-corrected accumulator.
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `SED` still sets `stepping=false`, so running will stop at decimal mode unless that remains an
2306e413 [gpt-5.6-terra] #intentional breakpoint.
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The `decimal` local in `sbc` is useful as a placeholder, but until its correction path exists it
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #may be helpful for the trace or breakpoint to show that decimal SBC has been encountered.
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Overall, the refactor has made the remaining work much safer: migrate each addressing mode to the
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #helper once, rather than duplicating arithmetic and flag behavior across every opcode.
2306e414 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
