2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #In `sbc(value)`, decimal handling belongs after calculating the unadjusted binary
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #subtraction and overflow, but before storing the result in A.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Conceptually, the helper has these stages:
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #1. Read A, operand, C, and D.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #2. Perform the existing binary subtraction internally as:
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `A + (~operand) + C`
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #3. Preserve that binary intermediate for:
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- overflow V;
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- NMOS decimal-mode N and Z;
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- no-borrow / carry determination.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #4. If D is set, adjust the intermediate result into packed BCD.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #5. Store the corrected low byte in A.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For SBC, the incoming carry is inverted in meaning:
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `C = 1`: subtract without borrowing.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `C = 0`: subtract with an extra borrow of one.
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #So the low-decimal-digit test must account for the incoming borrow. In terms of decimal digits:
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e681 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #low A digit - low operand digit - (1 - C)
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #If that value is negative, the low BCD digit borrowed from the high digit, so the binary
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #intermediate needs a decimal correction of `- $06`.
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Then, if the entire unadjusted subtraction borrowed—equivalently, the binary SBC intermediate has
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #no carry-out—you apply the high-digit correction of `- $60`.
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Examples, with D set:
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭─────────┬───────────┬───────────┬──────────────────┬────────────╮
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  A      │  Operand  │  Input C  │  Decimal result  │  Output C  │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #├─────────┼───────────┼───────────┼──────────────────┼────────────┤
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│ ---     │ ---:      │ ---:      │ ---:             │ ---:       │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$42`  │  `$17`    │  1        │  `$25`           │  1         │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$10`  │  `$01`    │  1        │  `$09`           │  1         │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$00`  │  `$01`    │  1        │  `$99`           │  0         │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$00`  │  `$00`    │  0        │  `$99`           │  0         │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$50`  │  `$01`    │  0        │  `$48`           │  1         │
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰─────────┴───────────┴───────────┴──────────────────┴────────────╯
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The last case demonstrates the input borrow: `50 - 01 - 1 = $48`.
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For valid packed-BCD values, your existing binary carry test:
2306e682 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #result > $ff
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #is also the correct no-borrow determination for decimal SBC. In the direct subtraction view, that
2306e683 [gpt-5.6-terra] #means:
