2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.245 345.4KB 5.90s
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The new `sbc` decimal block currently applies ADC-style corrections, so it needs adjustment
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #before use.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Problems in the current helper:
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `nibble` uses addition. For SBC it must represent low-digit subtraction, including borrow:
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- low A digit minus low operand digit minus `(1 - carry)`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A low-nibble borrow requires a subtract `06` correction, not `+ 06`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- An overall decimal borrow requires a subtract `60` correction, not `+ 60`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Carry/no-borrow should be derived from the original binary `diff`, not the BCD-adjusted `result`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- V must use `diff`, the binary intermediate—not `result`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A currently receives `diff & ff`; it needs to receive the BCD-corrected `result & ff`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- NMOS N/Z should come from `diff & $ff`, which is consistent with how your `adc` helper uses
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`sum`.
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The intended flow is:
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa39 [gpt-5.6-terra] #1. Calculate `diff = A + (~value) + C`.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #2. Determine binary no-borrow from `diff > $ff`.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #3. Calculate overflow from `A`, original `value`, and `diff`.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #4. If decimal mode:
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- inspect `lowA - lowValue - (1 - C)`;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- if negative, subtract `$06` from the result;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- if the binary subtraction borrowed (`diff <= ff`), subtract `60`.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #5. Set C from the binary no-borrow condition.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #6. Store corrected `result` in A.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #7. Set N/Z from `diff & $ff`.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #For example, decimal `10 - 01` with C set:
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- binary `diff` low byte is `$0F`;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- low nibble needs a borrow correction;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- subtract `$06`;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A becomes `$09`;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- C remains set.
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #And decimal `00 - 01` with C set:
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- binary low byte is `$FF`;
2306fa3a [gpt-5.6-terra] #- low correction applies;
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #- overall borrow applies, so subtract `$60`;
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #- A becomes `$99`;
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #- C clears.
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #Your `adc` helper is still correct; this issue is limited to translating its correction structure
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #directly into `sbc`.
2306fa3b [gpt-5.6-terra] #
