230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.054 56.78KB 14.07s
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #I reviewed `machine.ts`. It is a compact, readable 6502/DVG work-in-progress, with useful trace
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #output and a sensible separation between CPU, vector generator, input, and display helpers.
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #A few issues stand out:
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- TypeScript consistency
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `Machine` assigns `cyclecount` and `hasDVG`, but neither is declared as a class field.
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `frameCount` and `wordSize` lack explicit types.
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `LABS(address)` has an implicit `any` parameter.
230ac966 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `dump(grid:[[]])` is too narrow for the `string[][]` passed by `buildMemcode`.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `stepping` is inferred as `boolean`, but assignments such as `stepping=1-stepping` produce a
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #number.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `reset()` requires four arguments, but the `R` key handler calls it with three.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- RTI status restoration is incorrect
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- The RTI path uses `st=(st & ~0x14) | 0x20`.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `0x14` clears both the Break and Interrupt Disable bits. RTI should restore the saved Interrupt
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Disable state; only Break should be treated as non-persistent. This can cause interrupts to become
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #enabled unexpectedly after every RTI.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Memory-mapped writes are bypassed in several instructions
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Some writes go through `writeAddress()`, but several write directly to `this.memory[address]`,
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #including:
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #		- `STA (Indirect),Y`
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #		- `LSR Absolute`
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #		- `INC Absolute`
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #		- `DEC Absolute`
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- This will become significant for I/O registers, including DVG-related behaviour, because those
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #writes will not receive central handling.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Timing is presently instruction-count based
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `tick()` always adds four cycles, although 6502 instruction timings vary considerably and
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #branches/page crossings have special timing.
230ac967 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- This is understandable while bringing the emulator up, but VBLANK, frame pacing, and game
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #behaviour will eventually need instruction-specific cycle counts.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Interrupt behaviour
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `interrupt()` logs “interupt blocked by flag I” every time a VBLANK occurs while interrupts are
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #disabled. That will be very noisy during normal execution.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- The VBLANK latch logic is reasonable as a first pass, although its timing will depend on the
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #fixed-cycle issue above.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- DVG implementation is intentionally preliminary
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `LABS()` currently only uses two bytes for the beam position and logs an uncertainty note in the
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #surrounding code.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `VEC()` and `SVEC()` decode/log words but do not yet render or update beam coordinates.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- The DVG call stack has no underflow/overflow checks, so malformed display lists could create
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #difficult-to-diagnose failures.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Small cleanup opportunities
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `block` in `writeAddress()` is unused.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `missingCodes` is never cleared, so repeated CRT refreshes may report the same codes
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #indefinitely.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- `readAddress()` stops the whole machine for any unimplemented POKEY address, which is useful for
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #diagnostics but may make incremental Atari support harder.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- There are a number of comments that still describe uncertainty or earlier experiments;
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #consolidating those once the hardware rules are confirmed would make the opcode implementation
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #easier to audit.
230ac968 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
230ac969 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The main correctness priorities appear to be: fixing RTI’s status restoration, routing all writes
230ac969 [gpt-5.6-terra] #through `writeAddress()`, resolving the TypeScript declaration/call mismatches, and adding
230ac969 [gpt-5.6-terra] #per-opcode cycle accounting.
230ac969 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
