23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.058 60.53KB 16.36s
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #A few notable issues stand out:
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `reset` arguments are mismatched. Its signature is `(address, nmi, reset, irq, vectors)`,
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #but initial startup calls:
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #  - `game.reset(entry, nmi, irq, reset, true)`
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #  - This swaps the IRQ and reset vectors.
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The `R` key reset call is stale and invalid. It supplies four arguments where five are
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #required, and passes `game.dvg.enabled` in the IRQ position. This should currently fail TypeScript
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #checking.
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `stepping` is declared as a boolean but assigned numbers through `stepping=1-stepping`.
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #That is a TypeScript type error and should be boolean toggling instead.
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `dump` has the wrong element type. It accepts `Array<Array<number>>`, while
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`buildMemcode` produces `string[][]`; both current calls to `dump(grid)` are incompatible under
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #type checking.
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd7 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `JSR` stack storage is off by one. With an initial `SP` of `FF`, the low byte is written
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #to `01FD` rather than `01FE`. `RTS` then reads its low byte from `$01FE`, so returns will generally
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #be corrupted.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `RTI` incorrectly clears the interrupt-disable flag.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #  `st=(st & ~0x14) | 0x20` clears both B (`10`) and I (`04`). RTI should restore I from the
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #pulled status; only the synthetic break/unused-bit handling should be adjusted.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The reset/interrupt-vector naming is confusing enough to invite the first bug. `pc[2]`
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #receives `irq`, `pc[3]` receives `reset`, while the caller uses variables in the opposite order.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Making the API accept a named vector object would make this much safer.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Several writes bypass `writeAddress`. For example, `STA (Indirect),Y`, `INC Absolute`,
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`DEC Absolute`, and `LSR Absolute` write `this.memory[...]` directly. That will become inconsistent
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #if memory-mapped write behaviour is expanded.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The emulator structure is otherwise quite approachable: opcode handlers are explicit, the memory
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #access abstraction is already in place, and the vector engine is cleanly separated from the 6502
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #core.
23375cd8 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
