234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #High-Resolution Graphics (“Hi-Res”)
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Resolution: 280 × 192 pixels
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Practical colors: 6 display colors plus black and white:
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Black
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- White
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Green
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Purple
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Blue
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Orange
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Color is artifact-based rather than stored as conventional RGB values. Available color depends on
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #horizontal pixel alignment:
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- One pixel alignment produces purple/green.
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- The other produces blue/orange.
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Adjacent pixels can appear white.
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #Hi-Res Mixed Mode
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Graphics area: 280 × 160 pixels
234ad67d [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Text area: Bottom 4 text lines, or 32 pixels high
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Commonly used for games and applications requiring status text.
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #Video Memory
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Text page size: 1 KB per page
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Hi-res graphics page size: 8 KB per page
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Standard Apple II supports:
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Two text/lo-res display pages
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #	- Two hi-res display pages, when sufficient RAM is installed
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #Notes on Variants
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The original Apple II and Apple II Plus use the standard 40-column and 280 × 192
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #graphics modes described above.
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The Apple IIe added features such as lowercase support and optional 80-column text.
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #- The Apple IIc and Apple IIGS provide further display capabilities, with the IIGS
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #supporting substantially higher-resolution color graphics.
234ad67e [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae153 [simon@midnightblue.local] memory locations of banks?
234ae214 [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.017 2.923KB 11.70s
234ae214 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For the standard Apple II display pages, the important memory ranges are:
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭──────────────────────────┬─────────────────┬─────────────────╮
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Display area            │  Page 1         │  Page 2         │
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #├──────────────────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┤
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│ ---                      │ ---:            │ ---:            │
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Text / Lo-Res graphics  │  `$0400–$07FF`  │  `$0800–$0BFF`  │
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Hi-Res graphics         │  `$2000–$3FFF`  │  `$4000–$5FFF`  │
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰──────────────────────────┴─────────────────┴─────────────────╯
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Text and Lo-Res
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Lo-res graphics share the same memory as text mode.
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Text / Lo-Res Page 1: `0400–07FF`
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Text / Lo-Res Page 2: `0800–0BFF`
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Each page is 1 KB, although not every byte necessarily corresponds to a visibly displayed character
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #or lo-res cell in the simplest linear sense.
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Hi-Res Graphics
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Hi-Res Page 1: `2000–3FFF`
234ae215 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Hi-Res Page 2: `4000–5FFF`
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Each hi-res page occupies 8 KB. The visible 280 × 192 image uses a non-linear/interleaved address
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #layout within that range.
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Apple IIe / Auxiliary Memory Banks
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #On an Apple IIe with 128 KB RAM, there is a main and an auxiliary 64 KB bank. The
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #same address ranges can exist in either bank:
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭───────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Mode                             │  Main bank address                                │  Auxiliary bank address                          │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #├───────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│ ---                               │ ---:                                              │ ---:                                             │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  40-column text, normal graphics  │  Usually main `$0400–$0BFF`, `$2000–$5FFF`        │  Available but normally not displayed            │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  80-column text                   │  Main + auxiliary `$0400–$07FF` or `$0800–$0BFF`  │  Each bank supplies alternating columns          │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Double Lo-Res                    │  Main + auxiliary text-page memory                │  Main/aux combine for greater horizontal detail  │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Double Hi-Res                    │  Main + auxiliary `$2000–$3FFF` or `$4000–$5FFF`  │  Main/aux combine for 560 × 192 output           │
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰───────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For 80-column text and double hi-res, the display circuitry uses both main and auxiliary RAM at the
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #same addresses.
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae216 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Language Card / Upper Memory Banks
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #On systems with a Language Card or equivalent Apple IIe banked RAM arrangement:
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `D000–DFFF` can refer to either of two switchable 4 KB RAM banks.
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- `E000–FFFF` is the common 8 KB portion of Language Card RAM.
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Normally, this region contains ROM; soft switches select RAM visibility and write enable.
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #So the usual Language Card organization is:
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭─────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Address range  │  Bank arrangement                                     │
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #├─────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$D000–$DFFF`  │  Bank 1 or Bank 2, selected by soft switch            │
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$E000–$FFFF`  │  Shared/common Language Card RAM                      │
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$D000–$FFFF`  │  ROM visible unless Language Card RAM is switched in  │
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰─────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The display page selection itself is controlled by video soft switches, not by changing these
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #memory addresses.
234ae217 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
