2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.175 180.2KB 11.29s
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #On an original Apple II, those locations are soft-switch addresses. Reading them causes
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #hardware side effects, but the byte returned is generally not a defined switch value.
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For the addresses in your trace:
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭───────────┬────────────────────────────╮
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Address  │  Read/write side effect    │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #├───────────┼────────────────────────────┤
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C050`  │  graphics mode             │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C051`  │  text mode                 │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C054`  │  display page 1            │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C055`  │  display page 2            │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C056`  │  low-resolution graphics   │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C057`  │  high-resolution graphics  │
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰───────────┴────────────────────────────╯
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b150 [gpt-5.6-terra] #So:
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C056	; select low-res graphics
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C054	; select display page 1
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C051	; select text mode
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #uses `LDA` only because a memory read is the mechanism that toggles the switch. The
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #accumulator value is not the purpose of the instruction.
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #What value does `LDA $C051` receive?
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Usually: the floating bus value.
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The original Apple II does not necessarily drive a deliberate byte onto the CPU data bus for these
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #reads. Instead, the CPU sees whichever bits are present on the shared bus at that moment. This is
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #commonly called the floating bus.
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Its value can depend on:
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- the current video scan position,
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- the byte currently being fetched for display,
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- screen-memory contents,
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- precise timing.
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b151 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Therefore, it is not reliably `00`, `FF`, or a documented status byte.
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #In this particular boot code, the values are discarded immediately:
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #FB33  LDA $C056
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #FB36  LDA $C054
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #FB39  LDA $C051
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #FB3C  LDA #$00
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Thus a simple emulator can safely:
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #1. apply the soft-switch state transition, and
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #2. return any stable placeholder such as `$00`.
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Your current behaviour, returning zero-filled `memory[C0xx]`, is sufficient for this part of boot
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #provided you add the mode side effects. The reset code does not care what was loaded into
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`A`, because `FB3C` overwrites it with zero.
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #A useful emulation model
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Keep an `openBus` byte:
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Whenever memory or ROM is read, update `openBus` to that byte.
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- When a soft-switch read has no defined data value, perform its state change and return `openBus`.
2358b152 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- For a minimal emulator, simply return `0` instead.
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The meaningful behaviour is the state change:
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C051 → textMode = true
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C050 → textMode = false
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C054 → page = 1
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C055 → page = 2
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C056 → highResolution = false
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C057 → highResolution = true
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Strictly, `C056/C057` choose low-res versus high-res graphics; when text mode is selected, the
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #graphics-resolution selection remains stored but does not determine what is visibly displayed.
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #So the concise answer is: real hardware returns an undefined floating-bus byte; the important
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #result of the read is switching video state, not the value placed in `A`.
2358b153 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
