2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.5 gpt-5.6-terra 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.202 183.4KB 24.00s
2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #On an original Apple II, `C000–C0FF` is the I/O page. It is not ordinary RAM. Some
2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #addresses are motherboard soft switches; others are delegated to expansion cards.
2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #For a 1977/Apple II Plus-style machine, the useful map is:
2358b8fe [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #╭─────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  Address        │  Function                               │  Typical read behaviour                                                                         │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C000`        │  Keyboard data                          │  Returns key ASCII in bits 0–6; bit 7 is set when a key is waiting                              │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C010`        │  Clear keyboard strobe                  │  A read clears keyboard bit 7; return value is not usually important                            │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C020`        │  Cassette output toggle                 │  Read or write toggles cassette-output state                                                    │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C030`        │  Speaker toggle                         │  Read or write toggles speaker state                                                            │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C040–$C04F`  │  Cassette / utility soft-switch region  │  Exact use depends on machine/revision; usually not essential for a text-only initial emulator  │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C050`        │  Graphics mode                          │  Read or write selects graphics                                                                 │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C051`        │  Text mode                              │  Read or write selects text                                                                     │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C052`        │  Mixed graphics/text                    │  Read or write enables mixed mode                                                               │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C053`        │  Full graphics                          │  Read or write disables mixed mode                                                              │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C054`        │  Display page 1                         │  Read or write selects page 1                                                                   │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C055`        │  Display page 2                         │  Read or write selects page 2                                                                   │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C056`        │  Low-resolution graphics                │  Read or write selects lo-res graphics                                                          │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C057`        │  High-resolution graphics               │  Read or write selects hi-res graphics                                                          │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C058–$C05F`  │  Annunciator outputs                    │  Board/revision-dependent external-output switches                                              │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C060`        │  Cassette input                         │  Bit 7 represents cassette input level                                                          │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C061`        │  Pushbutton 0                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C062`        │  Pushbutton 1                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C063`        │  Pushbutton 2                           │  Bit 7 is set while button is pressed                                                           │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C064`        │  Paddle 0 timer                         │  Bit 7 remains set until paddle timer expires                                                   │
2358b8ff [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C065`        │  Paddle 1 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C066`        │  Paddle 2 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C067`        │  Paddle 3 timer                         │  Same                                                                                           │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C070`        │  Paddle trigger                         │  Read or write starts/recharges paddle timers                                                   │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C080–$C08F`  │  Language Card soft switches            │  Present only when a Language Card / compatible expansion is installed                          │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #│  `$C090–$C0FF`  │  Expansion-slot I/O                     │  Slot-specific registers; 16 addresses per slot                                                 │
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #╰─────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Keyboard: the first important missing device
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For BASIC to become interactive, implement `C000` and `C010`.
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The Apple II keyboard protocol is:
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C000:
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	bit 7 = 1 when a key is available
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	bits 0–6 = 7-bit key code
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #read $C010:
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	clear bit 7 of the keyboard latch
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b900 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For example, when `A` is typed:
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C000 returns $C1    ; $80 ready flag | $41 ASCII "A"
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #After the monitor consumes it by touching `$C010`:
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C000 returns $41    ; no pending-key flag
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The monitor input routine normally waits with logic equivalent to:
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #wait:
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	LDA $C000
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	BPL wait	; wait until bit 7 is set
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	...
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	BIT $C010	; clear keyboard strobe
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Your current input handling is Atari-oriented:
2358b901 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #if(block==0xc00){
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	const byte=this.input[address&3];
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #	return byte;
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #}
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #That means `C000`, `C001`, `C002`, `C003`, and also `C010` currently come from the same four-byte
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #input array via `address & 3`. For Apple II support, `C000` and `$C010` need distinct handling
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #before that generic Atari block logic.
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Speaker: `$C030`
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Every access toggles the speaker state:
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C030
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #or:
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b902 [gpt-5.6-terra] #STA $C030
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Both toggle it. There is no “speaker on” address and “speaker off” address. Software creates a tone
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #by touching `$C030` at a regular interval.
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For an initial emulator:
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- toggle a `speakerLevel` boolean;
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- optionally record the cycle count of each transition;
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- later translate transition timing into audio samples.
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The monitor boot trace has already entered `BELL`, and `BELL` eventually uses this mechanism.
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Display switches: `C050–C057`
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #These are the switches already visible in the trace:
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C056	; select lo-res graphics mode
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C054	; select text page 1
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C051	; select text mode
2358b903 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Representing the state separately is enough:
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #textMode: true / false
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #mixedMode: true / false
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #page2: true / false
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #hiRes: true / false
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Although both reads and writes activate the switch, the monitor conventionally uses reads.
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Game input: `C061–C070`
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Apple paddles are timed analogue inputs, rather than byte-valued registers.
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #A program triggers all paddle timers:
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C070
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b904 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Then polls, for example, paddle 0:
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #LDA $C064
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #BMI still_charging
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- bit 7 stays high while the simulated timer is active;
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- bit 7 becomes low after a duration corresponding to paddle position.
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #A minimal implementation can return `$00` for all paddle reads, which represents a paddle timer
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #that has already expired. That avoids hangs in software that waits for it.
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Pushbuttons are simpler:
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C061: button 0 in bit 7
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C062: button 1 in bit 7
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C063: button 2 in bit 7
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Expansion slots: `C090–C0FF`
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b905 [gpt-5.6-terra] #These ranges depend on the card installed in each physical slot:
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C090–$C09F  slot 1 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0A0–$C0AF  slot 2 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0B0–$C0BF  slot 3 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0C0–$C0CF  slot 4 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0D0–$C0DF  slot 5 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0E0–$C0EF  slot 6 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C0F0–$C0FF  slot 7 I/O
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The conventional Disk II controller is usually in slot 6, so DOS-related software accesses
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`C0E0–C0EF`. Those registers control drive selection, motor state, head phases, read mode, write
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #mode, and nibble data.
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Slot ROMs appear immediately above the I/O page:
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C100–$C1FF  slot 1 ROM
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #...
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C600–$C6FF  slot 6 ROM, commonly Disk II boot ROM
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #...
2358b906 [gpt-5.6-terra] #$C700–$C7FF  slot 7 ROM
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #The reset monitor can scan these ROMs to find bootable cards. So when you eventually emulate
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #booting from Disk II, you need both the slot-6 ROM at `C600–C6FF` and Disk II I/O behaviour at
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`C0E0–C0EF`.
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Language Card: `C080–C08F`
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #These switches belong to the optional 16 KiB Language Card, commonly present in Apple II Plus
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #systems running Applesoft BASIC.
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #They control RAM/ROM banking and write-enable status for the `D000–FFFF` region. The access pattern
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #is deliberately odd: certain reads switch banks; paired accesses can enable writes.
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #You do not need to implement this merely to run Integer BASIC and the monitor ROM shown in the
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #trace. It becomes necessary when:
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- the ROM configuration uses a Language Card,
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- Applesoft is loaded into language-card RAM,
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #- DOS or a boot loader banks RAM over ROM.
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #Practical implementation order
2358b907 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #For the machine currently booting in the trace, the highest-value order is:
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #1. `C000` keyboard latch and `C010` strobe clear
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Required to interact with the monitor/BASIC.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #2. `$C030` speaker toggle
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Required for an authentic boot bell, though it can initially be silent.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #3. `C050–C057` display soft-switch state
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Required to render the correct display mode/page.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #4. Text page memory rendering
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Page 1 starts at `0400`; page 2 starts at `0800`.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Apple II text rows are not linearly arranged in memory.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #5. `C061–C070` buttons and paddles
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Needed for games.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #6. Slot 6 Disk II I/O (`C0E0–C0EF`)
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #   Needed for disk booting and DOS.
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #One architecture point: rather than testing only `address & 0xFF00 === 0x0C00`, dispatch the full
2358b908 [gpt-5.6-terra] #`C000–C0FF` address through an Apple-II-specific I/O handler. The same page is used very
2358b909 [gpt-5.6-terra] #differently by the Atari ROMs, so the active machine profile should decide which device bus owns
2358b909 [gpt-5.6-terra] #it.
2358b909 [gpt-5.6-terra] #
