2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #Yes, the original Apple II and Apple II+ (which your emulator likely targets) had no lowercase
2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #letters in hardware. Instead, they used inverse uppercase (white on black) by setting bit 7
2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #of the character code. The standard character set maps codes `00`–`7F` to normal
2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #uppercase/graphics, while `80`–`FF` show the inverse (and sometimes flashing) version of
2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #those same characters.
2374eecd [deepseek-v4-flash] #
