23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #On the 6502, opcode $41 (decimal 65) is:
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #• `EOR ($nn, X)`*
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #• EOR with indirect, X* addressing.
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Bytes: 2
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Cycles: 6
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Operation: `A ← A XOR M`
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #  - Fetch a zero-page pointer from `(operand + X)` (wrapped in zero page).
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #  - Read the byte at that 16-bit address.
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #  - XOR it with the accumulator.
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Flags affected: N, Z
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #It is not to be confused with `$41` on some other 8-bit CPUs; on a standard 6502 it is always `EOR
23b4e96f [kimi-k2.7-code] #(indirect,X)`.
