23f36728 [simon@midnightblue.local] with applesoft roms i want emulate a soft reset in my emu
23f36801 [gemini-3.6-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.9 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.016 536B 13.18s
23f36801 [gemini-3.6-flash] #To emulate a soft reset (equivalent to pressing Ctrl+Reset on a physical Apple II) with Applesoft
23f36801 [gemini-3.6-flash] #ROMs, you need to replicate how the Apple II System Monitor and memory vectors handle the reset
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #sequence.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Key Memory Locations
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `FFFC` / `FFFD`: 6502 Hardware Reset Vector. Points to the System Monitor reset handler,
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #typically `$FA62`.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `03F2` / `03F3` (`SOFTEV`): Soft Reset Vector (Low/High byte). Holds the target memory
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #address to jump to on a soft reset.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `$03F4` (`POWERUP`): Reset Validation Checksum byte.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `$E000`: Applesoft BASIC Cold Start.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `$E003`: Applesoft BASIC Warm Start (retains the program in memory).
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #How the Soft Reset Sequence Works
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #When a reset is triggered, the CPU fetches the address from `FFFC-FFFD` and execution starts at
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #`$FA62` in the ROM Monitor. The Monitor determines whether to perform a Soft Reset (Warm
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Start) or a Hard Reset (Cold Boot) using the following validation check:
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. The Monitor calculates an expected validation byte:
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #   \textExpected Value = \textRAM[\$03F3] \oplus \$A5
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. It compares this calculated value with the byte stored at `RAM[$03F4]`.
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. If `RAM[03F4]` matches: The reset vector is valid. The Monitor executes an indirect jump
23f36802 [gemini-3.6-flash] #to the address stored in `03F2-03F3` (`JMP (03F2)`).
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #4. If `RAM[03F4]` does not match: The vector is invalid or corrupted (e.g., after
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #power-up). The Monitor initializes system hardware, sets up standard vectors, and performs a cold
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #boot (usually booting disk or starting Applesoft Cold Start at `E000`).
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #When DOS, ProDOS, or Applesoft BASIC is running normally:
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `03F2-03F3` is typically set to point to the DOS/ProDOS re-entry vector or Applesoft Warm Start
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #(`$E003`).
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• `03F4` is set to `HighByte(03F3) ^ $A5` to validate the soft reset vector.
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Implementation Strategies in Your Emulator
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Depending on how low-level your CPU and system emulation is, you can choose one of two approaches:
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Approach 1: Low-Level / Accurate Emulation (Recommended)
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Trigger a hardware reset on your emulated 6502 CPU.
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. Assert the CPU Reset line or set the CPU Program Counter (`PC`) to the 16-bit address stored at
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #vector `FFFC` (typically `FA62`).
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. Clear the interrupt disable flag if necessary, reset stack pointer logic as the 6502 hardware
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #does, and resume execution.
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. Let the original ROM execution at `FA62` evaluate `03F2–$03F4` and jump to the warm start vector
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #automatically.
23f36803 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #This ensures full fidelity with native hardware behavior and handles DOS, ProDOS, and custom
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #software hooks without special-casing.
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Approach 2: High-Level Vector Override (Fast / Shortcut)
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #If you wish to bypass running the Monitor reset code directly:
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. Read `RAM[03F3]` and `RAM[03F4]`.
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. Compute `val = RAM[$03F3] ^ 0xA5`.
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. If `val == RAM[$03F4]`:
23f36804 [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * Set CPU `PC = RAM[03F2] | (RAM[03F3] << 8)`
