23f37e6b [simon@midnightblue.local] what is prodos?
23f37efb [gemini-3.6-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.9 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.011 3.796KB 8.61s
23f37efb [gemini-3.6-flash] #• ProDOS (Professional Disk Operating System) is the operating system introduced by Apple
23f37efb [gemini-3.6-flash] #Computer in 1983 for the Apple II family of computers. It was designed to replace the aging DOS
23f37efb [gemini-3.6-flash] #3.3*, providing a more modern, faster, and expandable system environment.
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #Key Features of ProDOS
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. Hierarchical Directory Structure
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * Unlike DOS 3.3, which used a flat file system (all files stored in a single list on the disk),
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #ProDOS introduced nested directories and subdirectories, similar to modern file systems (MS-DOS,
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #Unix, macOS).
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. Support for Larger Storage Media
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * DOS 3.3 was strictly tailored to 140 KB 5.25-inch floppy disks (Disk II).
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * ProDOS natively supported larger media, including 3.5-inch floppies (800 KB), hard drives, and
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #RAM disk expansions, with volume sizes up to 32 Megabytes.
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. Standardized API: The Machine Language Interface (MLI)
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * ProDOS provided a uniform entry point (`JSR $BF00`) for software to perform disk I/O, file
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #operations, and memory management. This eliminated the need for developers to bypass the OS or
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #address hardware directly.
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #4. Improved Performance
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * Disk read and write operations under ProDOS were significantly faster than under DOS 3.3 due
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #to optimized block-based transfer routines.
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efc [gemini-3.6-flash] #5. Interoperability with BASIC
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * ProDOS separated the core operating system kernel from the user environment. To run Applesoft
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #BASIC programs, ProDOS loaded a system program named `BASIC.SYSTEM`, which translated traditional
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #Applesoft disk commands (such as `CATALOG`, `BLOAD`, and `RUN`) into ProDOS MLI calls.
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #ProDOS Versions
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #• ProDOS 8: Designed for 8-bit Apple II computers (Apple II Plus with 64K, Apple IIe, IIc,
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #and IIc Plus).
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #• ProDOS 16 / GS/OS: Designed for the 16-bit Apple IIGS, providing full support for the
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #65816 processor and advanced system architecture.
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #Relevance to Emulator Development
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #When emulating an Apple II system running ProDOS:
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Soft Reset Handling: ProDOS hooks the Soft Reset vector (`03F2–03F4`) during boot. When a
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #soft reset occurs, execution vectors back into the ProDOS system handler to restore the command
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #interpreter or System Selector safely.
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Storage Emulation: Implementing block-level storage devices (such as SmartPort or ProDOS
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #hard disk drives) allows your emulator to boot ProDOS directly from virtual hard drive images
23f37efd [gemini-3.6-flash] #(`.2MG`, `.HDV`, or `.PO` format).
23f37efe [gemini-3.6-flash] #
