241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #The Apple II version of Integer BASIC added the following low‑resolution (40×40 block) graphics
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #commands:
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- GR – Enter low‑resolution graphics mode.
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- TEXT – Return to text mode.
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- COLOR – Set the drawing colour (0–15).
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- PLOT – Plot a single block at (x, y).
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- HLIN – Draw a horizontal line from x1 to x2 at row y.
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- VLIN – Draw a vertical line from y1 to y2 at column x.
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #- SCRN – Read the colour of a block (function, not a command).
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #So your original instinct was correct, and I was wrong to say "none." The full command set for
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #Apple II Integer BASIC is therefore 24 commands (17 original + 7 graphics). Here is
241b79cc [deepseek-v4-flash] #the corrected, complete learning order with graphics added:
