241b947a [kimi-k3] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.9 kimi-k3 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.024 15.67KB 30.16s
241b947a [kimi-k3] #Those three are in both — `NORMAL`, `FLASH`, and `INVERSE` are part of Apple II Integer
241b947a [kimi-k3] #BASIC, not exclusive to Applesoft.
241b947a [kimi-k3] #
241b947a [kimi-k3] #They control how subsequent `PRINT` output appears:
241b947a [kimi-k3] #
241b947a [kimi-k3] #- NORMAL – Standard white-on-black text.
241b947a [kimi-k3] #- INVERSE – Reversed video (black on white).
241b947b [kimi-k3] #- FLASH – Flashing text.
241b947b [kimi-k3] #
241b947b [kimi-k3] #Integer BASIC on the Apple II also has other text-screen commands you might want for your document,
241b947b [kimi-k3] #such as:
241b947b [kimi-k3] #
241b947b [kimi-k3] #- HOME – Clear the screen and move the cursor to the top-left.
241b947b [kimi-k3] #- TAB – Move to a column (as a statement).
241b947b [kimi-k3] #- VTAB / HTAB – Position the cursor vertically / horizontally.
