241e5784 [kimi-k3] #🟠nitrologic Relay 1.9.9 kimi-k3 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.294 326.1KB 37.57s
241e5784 [kimi-k3] #The nibble lookup is in and correctly built — `appleANSI` maps index → 256-palette colour,
241e5784 [kimi-k3] #`initAppleBlocks()` precomputes all 256 escape strings with low nibble as the `▀` foreground and
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #high nibble as background, and it's now called before `runMachine()`. `gameRom` is flipped to
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #`apple2` too. That all looks right.
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #What remains unconnected, in dependency order:
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #• 1. Soft-switch state.* Nothing records which mode the machine is in. You need flags on
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #`Machine`, e.g.:
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #gfxText = true;      // $C051 text vs $C050 graphics
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #gfxMixed = true;     // $C053 mixed vs $C052 full
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #gfxPage2 = false;    // $C055 vs $C054
241e5785 [kimi-k3] #gfxHires = false;    // $C057 vs $C056
